.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt ERR_NEW 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ERR_new ,
.Nm ERR_set_debug ,
.Nm ERR_set_error ,
.Nm ERR_vset_error
.Nd Error recording building blocks
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/err.h
.Ft void
.Fo ERR_new
.Fa void
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo ERR_set_debug
.Fa "const char *file"
.Fa "int line"
.Fa "const char *func"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo ERR_set_error
.Fa "int lib"
.Fa "int reason"
.Fa "const char *fmt"
.Fa ...
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo ERR_vset_error
.Fa "int lib"
.Fa "int reason"
.Fa "const char *fmt"
.Fa "va_list args"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The functions described here are generally not used directly, but rather
through macros such as
.Xr ERR_raise 3 .
They can still be useful for anyone that wants to make their own macros.
.Pp
.Fn ERR_new
allocates a new slot in the thread's error queue.
.Pp
.Fn ERR_set_debug
sets the debug information related to the current error in the thread's
error queue.
The values that can be given are the filename
.Fa file ,
line in the file
.Fa line
and the name of the function
.Fa func
where the error occurred.
The names must be constant, this function will only save away the
pointers, not copy the strings.
.Pp
.Fn ERR_set_error
sets the error information, which are the library number
.Fa lib
and the reason code
.Fa reason ,
and additional data as a format string
.Fa fmt
and an arbitrary number of arguments.
The additional data is processed with
.Xr BIO_snprintf 3
to form the additional data string, which is allocated and store in the
error record.
.Pp
.Fn ERR_vset_error
works like
.Fn ERR_set_error ,
but takes a
.Vt va_list
argument instead of a variable number of arguments.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
ERR_new, ERR_set_debug, ERR_set_error and ERR_vset_error do not return
any values.
.Sh NOTES
The library number is unique to each unit that records errors.
OpenSSL has a number of preallocated ones for its own uses, but others
may allocate their own library number dynamically with
.Xr ERR_get_next_error_library 3 .
.Pp
Reason codes are unique within each library, and may have an associated
set of strings as a short description of the reason.
For dynamically allocated library numbers, reason strings are recorded
with
.Xr ERR_load_strings 3 .
.Pp
Provider authors are supplied with core versions of these functions, see
.Xr provider-base 7 .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ERR_raise 3 ,
.Xr ERR_get_next_error_library 3 ,
.Xr ERR_load_strings 3 ,
.Xr BIO_snprintf 3 ,
.Xr provider-base 7
